# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment hygiene.
#
# The two big exclusions are deliberate, not laziness:
#
#  *.joblib   trained models are ~55 MB AND are pickles, valid only against the
#             library versions that wrote them. Shipping them is the usual way a
#             working app dies on a host. The app rebuilds them in ~20 s from the
#             committed dataset instead.
#
#  the 8.7 MB master CSV  is regenerated by the pipeline; the gzipped 3.1 MB
#             copy under data/ is what gets committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.joblib
textile_dyeing_scaleup_master.csv

# Client source material - not ours to publish
*.pdf
WhatsApp*.jpeg
ZXCV-.123.xlsx
ruwan*.xlsx
data/factory_jobcard_template.xlsx

# Generated locally, not needed by the app
outputs/figures/fig0[1-6]*.png
outputs/figures/*.new.png
outputs/*.log
data/textile_dyeing_scaleup_factory_format.csv
outputs/tables/*.new.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# The mill's raw shade workbook. The app does not need it: build_shade_master()
# returns the cached data/shade_master.csv without ever opening the xlsx.
# Keeping the original out of the repo limits how much client source material
# is published, which matters if the repo is ever made public.
500_Textile_Dyeing_Shades.xlsx
data/500_Textile_Dyeing_Shades.xlsx
